<title>USA: Praxair to divest gas plants-US regulators.</title>
<headline>Praxair to divest gas plants-US regulators.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Trade Commission said it approved plans by Praxair Inc to sell four industrial gas-producing plants to AGA Gas Inc of Independence, Ohio.</p>
<p>The divestiture was required under a consent order aimed at restoring competition in production markets for certain merchant atmospheric gases after Danbury, Conn.-based Praxair bought CBI Industries Inc.</p>
<p>The plants are located in Bozrah, Conn.; Madison, Wisc.; Irwindale, Calif.; and Vacaville, Calif.</p>
</text>
